  "tagline": "LinkedIn's discontinued open-source Dynamo clone, retired in favour of Venice.",
  "description": "Voldemort was LinkedIn's distributed key-value store, one of the first open-source implementations of Amazon's Dynamo paper, with consistent hashing, vector-clock versioning, pluggable storage engines and a well-known read-only mode for bulk-loading Hadoop output. It served LinkedIn features such as 'People You May Know' for years. LinkedIn stopped all production use in 2018 and the README states the project is no longer under development; the read-only use cases moved to Venice. It is of historical interest only.",
